.TH PBS-ZABBIX-BACKUP-CHECK 1 "" "pbs-zabbix" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pbs\-zabbix\-backup\-check \- Zabbix UserParameter helper for Proxmox Backup Server task history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pbs-zabbix-backup-check
discovery
.br
.B pbs-zabbix-backup-check
age
.I vmid
.br
.B pbs-zabbix-backup-check
status
.I vmid
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads Proxmox Backup Server task logs from
.I /var/log/proxmox-backup/tasks
(world\-readable, no root or PBS API access required) and reports, per
VM/CT, backup freshness for Zabbix low\-level discovery and items.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B discovery
Print a Zabbix low\-level discovery JSON document listing
.B {#VMID}
for every VM/CT that has at least one recorded backup task.
.TP
.BI age " vmid"
Print the number of seconds since the last successful
.RI ( "TASK OK" )
backup task for
.IR vmid .
Prints a large sentinel value (999999999) if no successful backup was
ever recorded, so a staleness trigger fires immediately.
.TP
.BI status " vmid"
Print the last line of the most recent backup task log for
.IR vmid ,
regardless of success or failure, for use as alert context.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
Intended to be wired into
.I /etc/zabbix/zabbix_agent2.d/pbs-backup.conf
via
.B UserParameter
directives.
.SH AUTHOR
Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>
